    "Kos has about 37,000 inhabitants and is the second most populous island of the Dodecanese after Rhodes. According to tradition, Hippocrates, regarded as the father of medicine, was born here in the 5th century BC. Outside the town are the ruins of the Asklepieion, a sanctuary of Asclepius, the god of medicine, where the sick came to be healed. Its great terraces were built and expanded mostly after Hippocrates' time, in the Hellenistic period; the idea that he founded a medical school there is a later extrapolation.",
