    "In the town square stands the “Plane Tree of Hippocrates”. Tradition says the physician taught his pupils beneath it. The present tree is of course much younger, a few centuries old rather than 2,400 years, and its heavy limbs are propped up on scaffolding. The Hippocratic Oath, still recited in adapted form by new doctors, comes from the body of texts attributed to his school.",
