    "Astypalaia, on the western edge of the Dodecanese, is shaped like a butterfly and has about 1,400 inhabitants. Its Chora, with white houses and windmills, climbs up to the castle of the Querini, the Venetian lords of the island, who knew it as Stampalia. In recent years the Greek government and the Volkswagen Group have been working to make it a “smart, green island”: cars are being replaced by electric ones with subsidies, shared and on-demand vehicles run, and energy is to come from a solar plant with battery storage.",
